# Delivery and Constraints

## Must ship

- Clean Python with `/frontend` and `/backend` separated.
- A Dockerfile per service and a root `docker-compose.yml`. `docker-compose up` starts the full stack.
- `README.md` with an architecture diagram (ASCII or image), a 2-minute build and run, why the AI framework was chosen (LangGraph, LangChain, CrewAI, ADK, LiveKit, or Pipecat), and sample curl or Postman requests.
- A pytest suite covering backend endpoints, tool calls, and RAG retrieval.
- A markdown walkthrough with screenshots of the UI in action.

## Zero cost

Use a local vector store (Chroma, FAISS, or Qdrant local) and a free-tier LLM key (OpenAI, Anthropic, or Groq) or local Ollama. Do not add paid cloud services.

```text
# Good
Chroma on disk + Groq or Ollama

# Avoid
Pinecone, Weaviate Cloud, or any metered vector API
```

## Quality

Prefer clear architecture and working features over UI polish. Use small modules, typed request and response models, and tools with explicit inputs and outputs.
